From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PUBLISH-FIX-101: the second look has never armed - one
 missing gate name

Every JUDGE FUNNEL line ever printed, on every deployment:
  SECOND LOOK: flow-only refusals 0 -> looks retaken 0 (armed 0, dropped 0)
The counter increments on the first line of the arming path, so the path
was never reached. Not tuning - a bug.

Deployment 77962d92, first three decisions, all NO_TRADE:
  top refusals: PRIOR_MID_RESPONSE_SMALL 3, RECLAIM_FI15 3, FI15 3,
                FI60_POSITIVE 3, FI15_FRESH_AT_D 3, PRIOR_FI_ABSORBED 2
Five of six were in SECOND_LOOK_FLOW_GATES. FI15_FRESH_AT_D was not, and
the test is refused.every(id => set.has(id)) - so one name threw the
chain away. Over 8,076 recorded refused looks FI15_FRESH_AT_D was the
companion of a flow refusal 2,307 times, DEPTH_HOLDS_80PCT_OF_BASELINE
1,173 times: the two largest reasons the feature was inert.

Both are facts about the decision INSTANT, not about the coin:
FI15_FRESH_AT_D is the same 15s buying-pressure measure as FI15 read at
D (already trusted as retryable in DATA_LOOK_GATES), and
DEPTH_HOLDS_80PCT_OF_BASELINE is the current 10bps bid notional vs the
frozen median. Three minutes later both are different numbers - the
whole premise of a second look.

Also: a chain ended by a structural refusal now NAMES the gate that
ended it (counters.secondLookEndedBy, bounded 32, counted only when a
flow gate was among the refusers), and fly.js prints it - plus
dataLooksScheduled, which was being counted and never reported. Silence
is what let a dead feature hide for four days.

Nothing structural entered the set; no threshold moved; the bound and
the same-level requirement stand; a retaken look is a fresh crossing
with a fresh durable lock and every gate at full strength.

Frozen change: judge digest 96f83523029c -> 5233617b47ae, all
6016f931e155 -> e35b54c87b63; execution and watch/watch.js unchanged.
Recorded as docs/JUDGE-PAPER-AUDIT.md 4.38. Fenced by
test/publish-fix-101-second-look-actually-arms.test.js (5).

